From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcrt: Implement _aligned_recalloc, _freea and related heap functions.

Heap functions that were spec stubs: _aligned_recalloc and
_aligned_offset_recalloc (an aligned realloc whose growth is zeroed, ENOMEM
on an overflowing count; msvcr80 and later, ucrtbase), _recalloc_crt,
_freea and _freea_s (free a _malloca block that carries the heap marker,
leave stack blocks alone), _set_malloc_crt_max_wait (keeps the value and
returns the previous one; the CRT does not retry failed allocations, which
stays a FIXME) and msvcr80/90 _get_amblksiz/_set_amblksiz.
